From 081e53c31ae46a64622ce5aac8fc2ee1ccabc779 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Mikula <student@example.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:57:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Fix SSHA: implement the round function from the approved
 diagram

The old round loop ran 8 rounds per byte with operations that are not in the
diagram (A += (A+B)&~D, B ^= C^E), updated A..E in place so later lines used
already-overwritten values, and fed the wrong operands into C, D and E. This
made the digest ignore most of the data it was given, so tampering with a
username, timestamp or stored hash went undetected.

Now one round per message byte, all five outputs computed from the old state:
  A'=E  B'=A  C'=(A>>2)+E  D'=(A>>2)^(B>>1)  E'=msg[i]+(B>>1)+((B&C)|(D&C))

Tests now passing (previously failing):
  T12 - digest covers loginTime and localLoginTime
  T17 - corrupting a middle entry is reported at that entry, no success banner
  T19 - modified username is detected
  T20 - modified timestamp (raw and broken-down) is detected
  T21 - modified stored hash (middle, oldest, head) is detected
  T25 - SSHA output matches an independent implementation of the diagram

Still failing (documented limitation of the approved algorithm, not a code bug):
  T11, T13 - a few single-bit changes cancel out inside the 8-bit SSHA state
             (about 1.5% of random bit flips leave the digest unchanged)
---
 hash.c | 20 +++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hash.c b/hash.c
index 5d1192c..f6321f2 100644
--- a/hash.c
+++ b/hash.c
@@ -9,17 +9,15 @@ unsigned char* SSHA(const unsigned char* msg, size_t length) {
     E = 76;
 
     for (size_t i = 0; i < length; i++) {
-        for (int round = 0; round < 8; round++) {
-            unsigned char g = (B & C) | (C & D);
-            unsigned char old_A = A;
-            A += ((A + B) & ~D);
-            B ^= (C ^ E);
-            E = (g + msg[i] + B) & 0xFF;
-            D = A ^ C;
-            C = (old_A + E) & 0xFF;
-            A = E & 0xFF;
-            B = old_A & 0xFF;
-        }
+        // One round per message byte, per the SSHA diagram. All five new values
+        // are computed from the OLD A..E, so snapshot them first.
+        unsigned char a = A, b = B, c = C, d = D, e = E;
+
+        A = e;
+        B = a;
+        C = (unsigned char)((a >> 2) + e);
+        D = (unsigned char)((a >> 2) ^ (b >> 1));
+        E = (unsigned char)(msg[i] + (b >> 1) + ((b & c) | (d & c)));
     }
 
     unsigned char* digest = (unsigned char*)malloc(DIGEST_SIZE * sizeof(unsigned char));
